sanctioned: this program exercises the Ipe.Db.Store fetch-one terminal `toMaybe` (query |> where |> orderDesc |> toMaybe) over a raw-column store on sqlite::memory:. Ipe.Db.Store is an Ipê-only addition with no counterpart in the reference backend, and Ipê emits Rust+sqlx while the reference emits a different backend, so a shared Main.ipe cannot run on both. Ipê's output is recorded as the correct reference. `toMaybe` is defined as `Task.map List.head (toList conn q)`: it forwards its generic row type to `toList` and captures it in no closure of its own body, so cross-call type-parameter-bound propagation is what carries `toList`'s `Send + Sync` obligation onto the forwarded row tvar — without it the emitted `to_maybe<T1>` lacked `Sync` and cargo-failed E0277 (`T1 cannot be shared between threads`) despite `ipe` reporting exit 0, an exit-0-then-cargo-fail SEAL break. The four output lines assert, in order: (1) a `where (eq "id" "p1")` query returns the matching row as `Just` (by-id:widget:30); (2) among many matches, `toMaybe` reads the FIRST ordered row — qty descending picks widget (30) over gizmo (9) (first-ordered:widget:30); (3) a query matching no row returns `Nothing` (miss:nothing); (4) a value containing "'; DROP TABLE products; --" binds as a positional parameter and is stored + retrieved LITERALLY (parameterisation, not escaping — the table is not dropped).
